course: dictionary
lesson: 7009
title: Parcel: many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A parcel is usually a thing wrapped in paper or put in a box so it can be sent or given to someone. The words around it give the clue: «A delivery drone carries a small parcel» is about something being sent to a place.
explain: The word can mean other things too. «A parcel of land» is a piece of land, and as a verb, parcel up means wrap something into a package, while parcel out means share something out in parts. Read the words around it and ask: what would fit here?
explain: Some people use parcels to trick you. «Texts about a parcel that could not be delivered are a very common scam.» If a message asks for your card details or a password, stop and check the official site, as adults do.
fact: A parcel is a thing wrapped in paper or put in a box so it can be sent.
fact: «Parcel of land» means a piece of land.
fact: «Parcel up» means wrap something into a package.
fact: «Parcel out» means share something out in parts.
fact: Children in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand play «pass the parcel» at birthday parties.
exercise: «A delivery drone carries a small parcel and lowers it down.» What is the parcel here? | *A thing wrapped up to be sent | A loud noise | A kind of birthday game | A piece of land
exercise: Ellie says «parcel out» means wrap something up. What does it really mean? | To lose something on the way | To wrap something up tightly | *To share something out in parts | To put a letter in the post
exercise: «They bought a parcel of land by the river.» What does parcel mean here? | A kind of wrapping paper | A game at a party | *A piece of land | A box for the post
test: «Parcel up» the presents before the party. What does parcel up mean? | Share something out in parts | Lose something on the way | Open a box slowly | *Wrap something into a package
test: Why should you check a text about a parcel on the official site? | Official sites are always wrong | Parcels only arrive on Sundays | *It might be a scam that asks for your card details | The site sells cheap sweets
exam: Maya reads this on an invitation: «Come and play pass the parcel!» What is pass the parcel? | A kind of scam text | A piece of land | A race to send post | *A party game where a present is passed around
